olysis of the chlorido complexes) and analytical grade octanol. Mix aliquots of stock solutions of iridium complexes Ir1-Ir4 in OSW and WSO in equal volume and shaken in an IKA Vibrax VXC basic shaker for 4 h at 500 g/min, 298 K, to allow partition at room temperature. The aqueous layer was attentively separated from the octanol layer for iridium analysis. Partition coefcients of metal complexes were calculated using the equation log P =log ([M]WSO/[M]OSW), where [M]WSO was obtained by subtraction of the metal content of the aqueous layer after partition from the metal content of the aqueous layer before partition."}]}